      "content": "Any of various small, round, or cylindrical devices usually of bone, wood, or metal on which threads are wound for use in textile fabrication. [Source: Getty AAT] | stout thread or twine such as is used for sewing or tying up packs or bundles (OED s.v. packthread); bottom: a core on which to wind thread; (also) a skein or ball of thread or yarn (OED s.v. bottom n. and adj. 24)"
